    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Sixty per cent of deaths in the paediatric age group occur due to injuries or accidents. Motor vehicles are involved in most such injuries, incidence of which can be reduced by using car seats for younger children and seat belts for grown-ups. In the home, 'walkers' are the most common cause of injury among infants and the use of such equipment must be strongly discouraged.\"",
